{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_workspace_layout_and_docking_architecture", "label": "Workspace Layout and Docking Architecture", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_td_72", "label": "TD-72", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Docking was a five-column three-row Grid with panels assigned to named slots at composition time; the arrangement the mock-ups show was unrepresentable, not missing features."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_adr_0095", "label": "ADR-0095", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_adr_0092", "label": "ADR-0092", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_adr_0064", "label": "ADR-0064", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_adr_0103", "label": "ADR-0103", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_workspacelayouttree", "label": "WorkspaceLayoutTree", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Arbitrary nesting, a leaf is always a tab group, immutable pure operations, proportional weights: four properties carry the whole design."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_layoutsplitnode", "label": "LayoutSplitNode", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_layouttabgroupnode", "label": "LayoutTabGroupNode", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only leaf; a single docked panel is a group of one so tabbing is ordinary, not a special case."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_floatinglayoutwindow", "label": "FloatingLayoutWindow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_panelpresentation", "label": "PanelPresentation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_docking_is_always_a_move", "label": "Docking Is Always a Move", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The panel is removed from wherever it is before insertion so a panel can never appear twice."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_normalisation", "label": "Normalisation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Collapses one-child splits and same-orientation nested splits after every edit; a test drives ten dock/undock cycles and asserts depth unchanged."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_workspacepaneldescriptor", "label": "WorkspacePanelDescriptor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The whole integration: no privileged centre slot, no per-panel code in model, renderer or drag logic; a registered panel gains every behaviour at once."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_workspacelayouthost", "label": "WorkspaceLayoutHost", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A total function from tree to visual tree; the renderer decides nothing so the visual tree cannot drift from the model."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_layouttabgroupview", "label": "LayoutTabGroupView", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_floatingpanelwindow", "label": "FloatingPanelWindow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_docktargetresolver", "label": "DockTargetResolver", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pure geometry with no Avalonia types returning one of five zones; a release outside every pane is the undock gesture."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_drag_threshold", "label": "Drag Threshold", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A press is not a drag until the pointer passes a threshold so clicking a tab selects it rather than re-docking it."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_layout_persistence_via_isettingsprovider", "label": "Layout Persistence via ISettingsProvider", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Application session state, deliberately not the engineering persistence authority: where someone put their panels is not engineering data."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_versioned_layout_dto", "label": "Versioned Layout DTO", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hand-written versioned DTO rather than polymorphic serialisation so renaming a node type cannot orphan every saved layout; reading is total and every bad input falls back."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_empty_versus_corrupt_root", "label": "Empty Versus Corrupt Root", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every panel closed and the saved root was corrupt both end with a null root, so they are distinguished explicitly rather than conflated."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_workspacelayoutmigration", "label": "WorkspaceLayoutMigration", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carries a returning user widths, visibility, collapse and pin state into the equivalent tree on first launch."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_architecture_iworkspacelayout_projection", "label": "IWorkspaceLayout Projection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/architecture/Workspace Layout & Docking Architecture.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A live projection of the tree rather than a stale second account; lossy for tabbing and floating by construction (TD-91)."}, {"id": "docs_architecture_workspace_layout___docking_archite